{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "rules": {
    "comparison": "Compare sets of typed components, ignoring array order, articles, case, punctuation around an evidence fragment, and ё/е. Explicit aliases below permit inflections and synonyms. Counts, object role, polarity/preference, condition kind, and attached object must match. Evidence fragments are validated against the source separately. Exact match requires equality of the entire component set and a valid extraction.",
    "same_name": "Number repeated object names in their grounded mention order. For a symmetric next_to relation, use textual order where both objects are explicitly mentioned; other relations retain their direction.",
    "ambiguities": "Compare ambiguity kind. The optional wording supplied as evidence must still be present in the query. Generic image/search wording is omitted from intended content.",
    "deterministic": "Use a fixed development vocabulary and literal word matches. Extract named subjects, a single immediately adjacent color or numeric qualifier, known styles/media/scenes, and an explicit background phrase. Return an empty structure when the baseline cannot find evidence.",
    "precision": "Use micro precision/recall/F1 on components. False additions include wrong scopes, polarity and quantities, even when the wording was present. A rejected plan contributes an empty prediction and is never an exact match. No implicit count follows from a singular article or plural noun."
  },
